# The visual mode.

=== v and d delete the selection (inclusive)
text:
|abcdef
keys: vlld
want:
|def

=== v backwards
text:
abc|def
keys: vhhd
want:
a|ef

=== V deletes lines
text:
one
|two
three
four
keys: Vjd
want:
one
|four

=== y in the visual mode yanks
text:
|foo bar
keys: veyP
want:
fo|ofoo bar
mode: vim/normal

=== o goes to the other end
text:
ab|cdef
keys: vllohd
want:
a|f

=== c in the visual mode
text:
|foo bar
keys: vecbaz<Esc>
want:
ba|z bar

=== iw in the visual mode
text:
foo b|ar baz
keys: viwd
want:
foo | baz

=== gv selects again
text:
|abcdef
keys: vl<Esc>$gvd
want:
|cdef

=== Esc leaves without changing
text:
|abc
keys: vl<Esc>
want:
a|bc
mode: vim/normal

=== U and u change case
text:
|abc def
keys: veU
want:
|ABC def

=== > shifts the lines
text:
|one
two
keys: Vj>
want:
	|one
	two

=== J joins the lines
text:
|a
b
c
keys: VjjJ
want:
a b| c

=== p replaces the selection
text:
|one two
keys: yiwwviwp
want:
one on|e

=== a block deletes columns
text:
|abcd
efgh
ijkl
keys: <C-v>jjld
want:
|cd
gh
kl

=== a block yank and P
text:
|ab
cd
keys: <C-v>jyx
want:
|b
cd

=== dot repeats a visual delete of lines
text:
|1
2
3
4
5
keys: Vjd.
want:
|5

=== a block's I types on every line
text:
|abc
abc
abc
keys: l<C-v>jjI-<Esc>
want:
a|-bc
a-bc
a-bc

=== a block's I leaves shorter lines alone
text:
a|bc
x
abc
keys: <C-v>jjI-<Esc>
want:
a|-bc
x
a-bc

=== a block's A pads shorter lines
text:
|abc
x
abc
keys: <C-v>jjlA!<Esc>
want:
ab|!c
x !
ab!c

=== $A appends at every line's end
text:
|abc
x
abcd
keys: <C-v>jj$A;<Esc>
want:
abc|;
x;
abcd;

=== a block's c replaces it on every line
text:
|abcd
abcd
keys: l<C-v>jlcX<Esc>
want:
a|Xd
aXd

=== a block insert is one undo step
text:
|abc
abc
keys: <C-v>jI-<Esc>u
want:
|abc
abc

=== a block insert repeats with .
text:
|ab
ab
ab
ab
keys: <C-v>jI-<Esc>jj.
want:
-ab
-ab
|-ab
-ab

=== $ in a block selects to every line's end
text:
|abcd
x
abc
keys: l<C-v>jj$d
want:
|a
x
a

=== r in the visual mode replaces every character
text:
|hello world
keys: verx
want:
|xxxxx world

=== r on lines keeps the line breaks
text:
|ab
cd
keys: Vjr-
want:
|--
--

=== r on a block
text:
|abc
abc
keys: l<C-v>jr*
want:
a|*c
a*c
